/// Public API documentation for the "Bisnis Online" backend.
///
/// The document is static Markdown authored from the current backend source.
/// It reads no actor state, so the mixin takes no parameters.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend's public API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    Text.join(
      [
        "# Bisnis Online — Backend API",
        "",
        "Backend canister for a single-user online-business bookkeeping app (UMKM selling",
        "on Shopee / Tokopedia / Lazada). It stores products, sales transactions,",
        "restocks, and a cash ledger, and derives dashboard aggregates from them.",
        "",
        "All monetary values are whole Indonesian Rupiah (`Nat`, no fractional unit).",
        "All timestamps are nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Int`, from `Time.now()`).",
        "Identifiers are monotonic `Nat` values assigned by the backend.",
        "",
        "## Authentication and authorization",
        "",
        "This is a **single-user** application. There is no login, no per-user data, and",
        "no role system. Every public method below is callable by any caller, including",
        "anonymous ones; the backend performs no caller-based access control on domain",
        "methods.",
        "",
        "The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at",
        "`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds",
        "the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal",
        "against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`).",
        "Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it",
        "expires.",
        "",
        "The platform-provided authorization mixin (`MixinAuthorization`) is included for",
        "platform bookkeeping only. Its `_initialize_access_control` entry point is not",
        "required before calling any domain method: the domain methods are ungated, so a",
        "caller never needs to register first.",
        "",
        "## Data model",
        "",
        "- **Product** — `{ id : Nat; name : Text; price : Nat; cost : Nat; stock : Nat }`.",
        "  `price` is the selling price, `cost` the latest purchase (modal) price, `stock`",
        "  the current available quantity.",
        "- **Transaction** — `{ id : Nat; date : Int; orderNo : Text; productId : Nat;",
        "  productName : Text; qty : Nat; total : Nat; status : Status }`.",
        "  `productName` is denormalised at creation time, so the record stays readable",
        "  even if the product is later deleted.",
        "- **Restock** — `{ id : Nat; date : Int; productId : Nat; productName : Text;",
        "  qty : Nat; cost : Nat; supplier : Text }`. `cost` is the purchase price per",
        "  unit.",
        "- **CashflowEntry** — `{ id : Nat; date : Int; entryType : EntryType;",
        "  amount : Nat; note : Text; source : EntrySource }`. `amount` is always a",
        "  positive magnitude; `entryType` carries the direction.",
        "",
        "### Encodings",
        "",
        "- `Status` is the variant `#baru | #proses | #kirim | #selesai`.",
        "- `EntryType` is the variant `#masuk | #keluar`.",
        "- `EntrySource` is the variant `#manual | #transaksi | #restock`.",
        "- Optional numeric inputs (`?Nat`) may be omitted; the backend defaults them to 0.",
        "- `Result.Result<Ok, Err>` is the Candid variant `#ok(Ok) | #err(Err)`.",
        "",
        "## Methods",
        "",
        "### Products",
        "",
        "- `createProduct(input : NewProduct) : async Result<Nat, ProductError>`",
        "  Creates a product. `name` is required and must be non-empty after trimming;",
        "  `price`, `cost`, and `stock` are optional and default to 0. Returns the new",
        "  product id, or `#err(#emptyName)`.",
        "- `listProducts() : async [ProductView]` — query. Every product with its derived",
        "  `sold` quantity (sum of `qty` over every transaction referencing it).",
        "- `deleteProduct(id : Nat) : async Bool` — deletes a product. Returns `false`",
        "  when no product has that id. Transactions already recorded keep their",
        "  denormalised `productName`.",
        "",
        "### Transactions",
        "",
        "- `createTransaction(input : NewTransaction) : async Result<Transaction, TransactionError>`",
        "  Creates a manual transaction. `total` is computed as `qty * product.price`.",
        "  On success the product's stock is decremented by `qty` and one cash-in entry",
        "  (`#transaksi`, amount = `total`) is appended to the ledger. Fails with",
        "  `#productNotFound`, `#invalidQty` (qty is 0), or",
        "  `#insufficientStock { available; requested }` when `qty` exceeds current stock.",
        "- `listTransactions() : async [Transaction]` — query. All transactions, newest",
        "  first.",
        "- `updateTransactionStatus(id : Nat, status : Status) : async Result<Transaction, TransactionError>`",
        "  Changes a transaction's status. **Does not change stock and does not create a",
        "  cash entry.** Fails with `#notFound`.",
        "- `importTransactions(raw : Text) : async ImportSummary`",
        "  Bulk import of a TAB-separated paste copied from a spreadsheet. Column order:",
        "  `Tanggal`, `No Pesanan`, `Nama Barang`, `QTY`, `Harga satuan`. The date must be",
        "  `DD-MonthName-YYYY` with an Indonesian month name (e.g. `29-September-2026`).",
        "  If a product name does not exist it is created automatically with",
        "  `price = unitPrice` and `cost = 0`, `stock = 0`. Imported transactions are",
        "  created with status `#selesai` and **do not change product stock** (they are",
        "  past sales). Each successful row still appends one cash-in entry. Returns",
        "  `{ succeeded; skipped; details }`, where `details` lists each skipped row with",
        "  its 1-based line number and reason (`#invalidRow`, `#invalidDate`,",
        "  `#invalidNumber`, `#emptyLine`).",
        "",
        "### Restock",
        "",
        "- `createRestock(input : NewRestock) : async Result<Restock, RestockError>`",
        "  Records a restock. On success the product's stock increases by `qty`, the",
        "  product's `cost` is **overwritten** with the new purchase price, and one",
        "  cash-out entry (`#restock`, amount = `qty * cost`) is appended. Fails with",
        "  `#productNotFound` or `#invalidQty` (qty is 0).",
        "- `listRestocks() : async [Restock]` — query. All restocks, newest first.",
        "",
        "### Cash ledger",
        "",
        "- `createCashflowEntry(input : NewCashflowEntry) : async Result<CashflowEntry, CashflowError>`",
        "  Records a manual cash movement for costs outside transactions and restocks.",
        "  Fails with `#invalidAmount` when `amount` is 0.",
        "- `listCashflow() : async [CashflowRow]` — query. Every cash entry (manual and",
        "  automatic) ordered by date ascending, ties broken by id ascending, each with a",
        "  running `balance` (`Int`) after that entry is applied.",
        "- `getCashBalance() : async Int` — query. Current total cash balance (all",
        "  cash-in minus all cash-out).",
        "",
        "### Dashboard",
        "",
        "- `getDashboard() : async DashboardData` — query. Returns",
        "  `{ summary; recentTransactions; lowStockProducts }`:",
        "  - `summary.omzet` — sum of every transaction `total`.",
        "  - `summary.labaKotor` — `omzet` minus cost of goods sold",
        "    (sum of `qty * product.cost` over every transaction); `Int`, may be negative.",
        "  - `summary.saldoKas` — cash-in minus cash-out; `Int`.",
        "  - `summary.produkStokMenipis` — number of products with stock <= 5.",
        "  - `recentTransactions` — the five most recent transactions, newest first.",
        "  - `lowStockProducts` — products with stock <= 5, lowest stock first.",
        "",
        "### Documentation",
        "",
        "- `getApiDoc() : async Text` — query. This document.",
        "",
        "## Lifecycle and polling",
        "",
        "Every method is a single request/response call; there are no long-running jobs,",
        "no background tasks, and no asynchronous completion to poll. A mutation is",
        "complete when its call returns. Read methods are `query` calls and can be polled",
        "freely.",
        "",
        "## Mutation retry safety",
        "",
        "Mutations are **not idempotent**. Retrying a call that already succeeded creates",
        "a duplicate record and, for `createTransaction` and `createRestock`, applies the",
        "stock change and the cash entry a second time. `importTransactions` is likewise",
        "not idempotent: re-submitting the same paste imports every row again. Only retry",
        "a mutation when the previous call failed or its outcome is unknown, and re-read",
        "the affected lists afterwards to confirm state.",
        "",
        "## Errors, traps, and gotchas",
        "",
        "- Domain failures are returned as `#err(...)` variants, not traps, so callers can",
        "  branch on them. A trap (opaque reject) indicates a broken invariant.",
        "- `createProduct` with an empty or whitespace-only `name` returns `#emptyName`.",
        "- `createTransaction` rejects `qty = 0` and any `qty` above the current stock.",
        "- **Bulk import does not change stock** — imported rows are historical and are",
        "  created as `#selesai`.",
        "- **Changing a transaction's status never changes stock** and never creates a",
        "  cash entry; stock and cash are affected only at creation time.",
        "- **Restock overwrites the product's `cost`** with the latest purchase price; it",
        "  does not average or keep history.",
        "- Deleting a product does not delete its transactions, restocks, or cash entries.",
        "- `labaKotor` and `saldoKas` are `Int` and can be negative.",
        "- Cash entries created automatically by transactions and restocks cannot be",
        "  edited or deleted through the public API.",
      ].values(),
      "\n",
    );
  };
};
